      "writtenOn": "2026-06-09T16:15:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally, global variables are frowned upon upstream and should be avoided. That being said, due to the nature of this change working around the KABI, this seems like a good approach.\n\nMy one concern is for maintainability- if some code is introduce which refactors something which uses udc, and does not check for it to be null, then we would be introducing a new UAF.\n\nLet\u0027s rename this `android_udc_state_lock` and add a comment above it:\n\n```\n/* \n * ANDROID: Global lock used instead of a per-gadget lock to maintain KABI \n * compatibility. Serializes state changes during gadget teardown.\n */\n```",
      "revId": "8918b8050a611229008cfaf71839764e5f565ce6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
